<section id="overview" aria-labelledby="t-overview">
<h2 id="t-overview">Course overview</h2>
<p>This course introduces artificial neural networks: how a neuron works, how networks learn, the main architectures (feedforward, CNN, RNN), and how to build and evaluate simple models in Python with Keras and TensorFlow.</p>
<div class="facts">
<div><b>Category</b>Discipline-Specific Elective-3</div>
<div><b>Teaching hours per week</b>4 lecture + 2 practical</div>
<div><b>Credits</b>5</div>
<div><b>Total marks</b>150 (Theory 100, Practical 50)</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> basic programming (preferably Python), elementary algebra and probability, and introductory machine learning and data analysis.</p>

<h3>Course outcomes</h3>
<p>After completing the course, you will be able to:</p>
